  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.to_directed - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.to_directed.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.to_directed()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Convert the graph to a directed graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.to_directed()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Convert the graph to a directed graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.to_directed()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Convert the graph to a directed graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nConvert the graph to a directed graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L49658-L49762){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.to_directed()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Convert to directed](../assets/graphs/to-directed.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"An undirected path A, B, C, D with three plain edges. After to_directed(), each undirected edge has become a pair of accent arrows, one in each direction, so the three edges become six.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nCreates a new graph with the same nodes but directed edges. If the graph is already\ndirected, returns a new copy. For undirected graphs, creates both directions (u->v and v->u)\nfor each edge.\n\nRepresenting each undirected edge as a pair of opposite arcs keeps reachability and\nshortest-path distances exactly as they were, while letting you treat the two directions\nseparately afterwards. Typical reasons to convert:\n\n- running an algorithm that only accepts directed graphs\n- starting from a symmetric network and then removing or reweighting one direction\n  (e.g., turning a two-way street into a one-way street)\n- combining the graph with a directed graph in set operations such as `union()` or\n  `compose()`, which require matching directedness\n\nNode IDs, labels, and node attributes are carried over unchanged. Both arcs created from\nan undirected edge get that edge's weight and attributes, so an undirected graph with\n`m` edges becomes a directed graph with `2m` edges. The arc in each edge's stored\ndirection keeps the edge's ID; the reverse arcs are new edges with fresh IDs, listed after\nall the originals. The original graph is not modified.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new directed Graph with the same nodes. Edges are bidirectional pairs if the original\n    was undirected, or unchanged copies if it was already directed.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~to_undirected`) \n\n:   Drop the direction of every edge.\n\n[](`~reverse`) \n\n:   Flip the direction of every edge.\n\n[](`~shortest_path_length`) \n\n:   The length of a shortest path, which can differ each way.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEach undirected edge becomes two directed edges, one in each direction:\n\n::: {#0ce4f3f2 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\")])\narcs = path.to_directed()\n\narcs.is_directed(), arcs.get_edges_str_repr(use_labels=True)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, ['A->B', 'B->C', 'B->A', 'C->B'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nBoth arcs keep the original edge's weight and attributes:\n\n::: {#fdd60f05 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nroads = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\", 5.0)])\n\nroads.to_directed().get_edge_df().select(\"source\", \"target\", \"weight\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (2, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>source</th><th>target</th><th>weight</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>i64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>5.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>5.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Works on one track\n\nA metro's tracks run both ways, so the network is undirected, and every trip takes as long\nas the trip back. From Westgate to Eastfield, either way, is 14 minutes. Turning each track\ninto a pair of one-way tracks makes it possible to close just one of them:\n\n::: {#2f27985a .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\nlines = metro.to_directed()\n\nmetro.count_edges(), lines.count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(25, 50)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWorks close the eastbound track from Central to Market. Trains still run west from Market\nto Central, so the trip from Eastfield to Westgate is unchanged, but the trip the other\nway now detours around the Ring line through Riverside and takes 2 minutes longer:\n\n::: {#ecaffd87 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nlines.delete_edge(\"Central\", \"Market\")\n\n(\n    lines.shortest_path_length(\"Westgate\", \"Eastfield\"),\n    lines.shortest_path_length(\"Eastfield\", \"Westgate\"),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n(16.0, 14.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#372bd76d .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\neast = lines.shortest_path(\"Westgate\", \"Eastfield\", return_list=True)\n\nlines.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\",\n    label_by=\"label\",\n    highlight=east,\n    highlight_edges=list(zip(east, east[1:])),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-